WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.769
Night drone operations are flights conducted after dark or under low-light conditions

00:00:04.769 --> 00:00:07.104
where normal visual cues are reduced.

00:00:07.104 --> 00:00:10.216
The aircraft may be technically capable of flying,

00:00:10.216 --> 00:00:14.107
but the operator's ability to judge position, orientation, distance, obstacles,

00:00:14.107 --> 00:00:16.831
and changing conditions is different from daylight.

00:00:16.831 --> 00:00:19.555
Aircraft lights can help identify the drone,

00:00:19.555 --> 00:00:24.224
yet they do not illuminate every hazard or preserve full depth perception.

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:26.169
Background lights, glare, darkness, haze,

00:00:26.169 --> 00:00:30.449
and uneven terrain can make the aircraft appear closer, farther, higher,

00:00:30.449 --> 00:00:32.784
or differently oriented than it is.

00:00:32.784 --> 00:00:35.507
Camera and navigation sensors also have limits.

00:00:35.507 --> 00:00:39.009
Low-light video may show noise, blur, or poor contrast.

00:00:39.009 --> 00:00:42.122
Obstacle sensors may depend on texture or illumination.

00:00:42.122 --> 00:00:46.402
A clear controller display does not guarantee that wires, branches, people,

00:00:46.402 --> 00:00:47.958
or aircraft are visible.

00:00:47.958 --> 00:00:49.125
Human performance matters.

00:00:49.125 --> 00:00:52.627
Night adaptation takes time, bright screens can reduce it,

00:00:52.627 --> 00:00:55.351
and fatigue can slow recognition and decisions.

00:00:55.351 --> 00:01:00.020
Crew communication and a simple mission plan help compensate for reduced perception.

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:02.744
Safety, legality, privacy, and accountability remain inseparable.

00:01:02.744 --> 00:01:05.856
Current aviation requirements, airspace, site permissions, aircraft lighting,

00:01:05.856 --> 00:01:10.525
visual-line-of-sight expectations, and local rules must be checked for the actual mission.

00:01:10.525 --> 00:01:13.249
Night is not merely a camera setting.

00:01:13.249 --> 00:01:15.584
It increases uncertainty and reduces margins.

00:01:15.584 --> 00:01:17.918
The responsible objective is a bounded,

00:01:17.918 --> 00:01:22.587
necessary flight that can be stopped early when visibility, orientation, weather, equipment,

00:01:22.587 --> 00:01:25.700
or crew performance no longer supports safe operation.
